From: openEuler RISC-V Maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] tests: use the target repository's Catch2 v3 interface

SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
Upstream-Status: Not Submitted [target test dependency compatibility]

The original suite used the v2 single header and CATCH_CONFIG_MAIN. Catch2
v3 supplies separate headers and an explicit main-providing dependency.
Keep every original test case, assertion, fixture, and default option.
The write executable keeps its own main and original catch2 dependency.
Remove when upstream tests support Catch2 v3 without this change.

--- a/tests/meson.build
+++ b/tests/meson.build
@@ -8,0 +9 @@
+catch2_main_dep = dependency('catch2-with-main')
@@ -96 +97 @@
-		       dependencies : catch2_dep)
+		       dependencies : catch2_main_dep)
--- a/tests/test-read.cpp
+++ b/tests/test-read.cpp
@@ -10,2 +10 @@
-#define CATCH_CONFIG_MAIN
-#include "catch2/catch.hpp"
+#include "catch2/catch_all.hpp"
